      "body": "# PR type\n- [x] Bug Fix\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [ ] Document Updates\n- [ ] More Models or Datasets Support\n\n# PR information\n\nFixes #10506\n\n`GLM5NextTemplate` (GLM-5.3-Flash) inherits `GLM5_2Template`, whose `reasoning_effort_needs_thinking = True` renders the `Reasoning Effort: ...` system line only when thinking is on. Thinking is off by default for this template, so by default every training row was encoded without the line. The GLM-5.3-Flash release `chat_template.jinja` writes it on every conversation (default Max), as GLM-5.3 does; `GLM5_3Template` already sets the flag to `False`. This PR sets the same flag on `GLM5NextTemplate`.\n\n## Experiment results\n\nToken comparison of ms-swift's encoding (training mode, `swift.dataset.load_dataset` + `get_template`) against the release template rendered by transformers' `apply_chat_template` from the `zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash` files, on 384 GSM8K rows (main `680df5c6`, transformers 5.18.0, CPU):\n\n| setting | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| default (no env, no template kwargs) | 384 / 384 rows differ | 0 differ |\n| `REASONING_EFFORT=low` | 384 / 384 rows differ | 0 differ |\n| `REASONING_EFFORT=low`, `enable_thinking=True` | 0 differ | 0 differ |\n\n\"0 differ\" means ms-swift's input ids equal the release rendering followed by the next `<|user|>` (the stop token ms-swift appends after the last assistant turn). The minimal example in the issue prints the same string as the release template after this change.\n\n# Checklist\n\n- [x] I have linked the related issue above, if there is one.\n- [x] I have reviewed and understand every changed line, and I can explain how the change works and why it is correct.\n- [x] I have run the relevant tests or reproductions locally, and included the commands and results above (if applicable).\n- [x] I am responsible for the content of this PR, regardless of how it was produced.\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
